      "note": "This is the portal's public sample key, so it is capped at five trains per line: what is drawn is a sample of the fleet, not the whole of it. The endpoint reports which station a train is at, never a position, so each train sits on its station's coordinate and a train at a station the table cannot resolve — or a name shared by two stations, such as 양평 — is not drawn at all. The sample key is limited to 1,000 requests a day for everyone together, so this feed is budgeted, not polled: pollSec / budgetSec / maxAgeSec are one contract (16 lines × 86400/1500 = 921 requests a day at worst, held for 40 minutes so a refused poll never blanks the map) and tests/transit.test.mjs fails if they are retuned apart. The browser makes one bounded relay call for all sixteen lines; the relay's fixed allowlist and per-line cache share each answer for budgetSec, so every visitor shares one request per window instead of spending the key per tab. Register a free key at data.seoul.go.kr and put it in `base` in place of `sample` for full coverage and a larger budget. Korean buses and the metro of Busan, Daegu, Daejeon and Gwangju publish no keyless feed, so they are absent."
